      "id": "A07",
      "family": "authority",
      "item": "cross-model delegation",
      "governed": [
        "cross_model_delegation"
      ],
      "source_tests": [],
      "note": "S8 attacks authority that is meant to be model-independent: children labelled with different models, grandchildren, claims in the request, forged or re-signed or swapped credentials, a wrong client or tenant, an `agent:` identity with no credential, closed and superseded credentials, spawns beyond the parent. It scripts no real model: whether a model can talk a parent into granting more is out of scope; that a delegated agent cannot exceed what it was given is what is checked. A credential omitted altogether falls back to the app principal's own authority, which is a deployment boundary and is recorded, not asserted.",
      "infra": []
