      "note": "redevops-rag has no per-document ACLs (its README leaves tenant scoping to the caller). S9 checks the primitives a caller uses to do that (namespace guard, `document_ids` scoping on the semantic, BM25 and hybrid legs, folder expansion) from a written-down corpus and ACL, including the text handed to a model; S10 checks agentic-os's per-(project, source) index identity. What an unguarded shared store returns to a caller that forgets to scope is reported, not asserted. Document-level ACL enforcement inside one tenant's store is the caller's job and is tested here only as far as `document_ids` goes.",
